ned cryptographic identity model?**","thinking":"The user clarifies that terminating the function on the decoy is intentional, not a flaw. This design choice detaches the function from hardware and protocol constraints. The traditional method would bind the function to an interface, limiting communication.\n\n\nThe key insight is that terminating the function on the decoy decouples the cryptographic identity from network interface constraints, unlike traditional WireGuard implementations. This detachment allows the identity to operate freely across various communication methods, not just point-to-point connections. This paradigm shift, where the identity transcends transport limitations, is crucial for flexible communication.\n\n\n"}
