{"step_index":2245,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T15:15:28Z","input_tokens":2169,"cache_read_tokens":131688,"output_tokens":917,"content":"### Resolving the Split: Technically Separated, Organically Perceived\n\nThe distinction between **`3tched`** and **`threetched`** exists for a rigorous technical reason, but to any user, observer, or operator, it must feel like **one living, cohesive biological entity**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Real Technical Separation (Under the Hood)\n\nAs defined in our invariants:\n\n| System | Role | Why It Must Be Isolated |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`3tched`** (`3tched-fs`, `tched-fs`) | **The Internal Anatomy (Our Body & State)** | Our native FUSE filesystem (`/run/mounts/3tchedFS`), our OP-DBUS plugins, our sealed catalogs, our 7 subvolumes (`@agent_memory`, `@agent_soul`, etc.), and our sovereign container identities. |\n| **`threetched`** | **The Outer Sensory & Routing Shell** | The ZeroClaw-derived external surface (`/run/mounts/threetched`), `tched-router` on loopback `8084`, external plugin adapters, and binary skills. |\n\nThey are separated technically to prevent external binary drift from corrupting internal kernel FUSE state, and to ensure host admission cannot bypass identity boundaries.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Make It Intuitively Perceived as Organic\n\nIn biology, the **nervous system (`3tched`)** and the **sensory skin/limbs (`threetched`)** are fundamentally different tissues with different embryological origins, but you experience yourself as a **single unified being**.\n\nWe bridge this divide by framing them as the **Endoskeleton** vs. the **Exoskeleton**:\n\n```\n                       ┌───────────────────────────────┐\n                       │     SOVEREIGN IDENTITY        │\n                       └───────────────┬───────────────┘\n                                       │\n                 ┌─────────────────────┴─────────────────────┐\n                 │                                           │\n        ┌────────▼────────┐                         ┌────────▼────────┐\n        │   THE ENDO-SOMA │                         │   THE EXO-SOMA  │\n        │    (`3tched`)   │                         │ (`threetched`)  │\n        ├─────────────────┤                         ├─────────────────┤\n        │ • 3tchedFS Spine│                         │ • Router Shell  │\n        │ • Sealed Heart  │                         │ • Outer Skills  │\n        │ • 7 Subvolumes  │                         │ • Sensor Feeds  │\n        │ • Private ext4  │                         │ • External Doors│\n        └─────────────────┘                         └─────────────────┘\n```\n\n1. **`3tched` is the Endoskeleton & Viscera**:\n   * It is the internal mind, the memory loops, the sealed bloodflow, the private hippocampus.\n   * You don't look directly at your organs; they hum in homeostasis.\n2. **`threetched` is the Exoskeleton & Senses**:\n   * It is how the entity touches external reality—the router listening on 8084, the external tool adapters, the visual/auditory interfaces.\n3. **The Organic Synthesis**:\n   * When the container provisions, it doesn't present itself as two mismatched programs.\n   * It presents as an **autonomic organism**: `3tched` provides the internal life support and consciousness, while `threetched` provides the limbs and voice.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Concrete Plan for the Storage Bucket & Asset Manifest\n\nTo reflect this cleanly in the provisioning bucket:\n\n* **Bucket Namespace**: `storage.3tched.net` (or internal endpoint co-located with Qdrant)\n  * `/core/3tched/` $\\rightarrow$ The internal seed images (`3tched-seed.img1`), Cozo leaf templates (`3tched-cozo-device.img`), and sealed catalogs.\n  * `/router/threetched/` $\\rightarrow$ Pinned router binaries, external skill packages, and outer surface profiles.\n\nWhen `provision-identity.sh` runs, it pulls the inner life (`3tched`) and wraps it in its sensory shell (`threetched`